{#
  index.html.j2  |  the front door  |  Phase W3

  EVERY LINE OF COPY ON THIS PAGE COMES FROM RULED MATERIAL. The two named layers
  are CLAUDE.md section 1. Each part's description is its Purpose line from
  AIOM_Structure_v1.md, parsed by book_structure.py rather than retyped. Chapter
  titles come from the same place, and gate W7 fails the build if a locked
  chapter's own title disagrees with it.

  What is deliberately NOT here: any chapter's "Big idea", "Competency" or
  "Anchor theorem" line. Those are internal planning shorthand, and CLAUDE.md
  section 9 rules that later chapters withhold things deliberately and must not be
  front-run by an earlier surface. A chapter is a title and a lock state here,
  nothing more.

  The framing copy is DRAFT and awaits Dan's ruling. It is marked as such in
  AIOM_Web_Edition_Plan_v1.0.md section 10 rather than presented as settled.
#}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-US">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>AI Operations Management</title>
<meta name="description" content="A founding textbook. AI Business Economics is the science. AI Operations Management is the practice discipline that acts on it.">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/aiom_web.css">
</head>
<body class="home">

<header class="topbar" data-chrome>
  <a class="brand" href="./">AI Operations Management</a>
  <nav class="topnav">
    <a href="#parts">The book</a>
    <a href="#read">Read</a>
    <a href="glossary/">Glossary</a>
    <a href="sources/">Sources</a>
    <a href="search/">Search</a>
  </nav>
  <a class="cta" href="#editions">Get the book</a>
</header>

<main>

  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">A founding textbook</p>
    <h1>Most organizations bought AI as software. They are operating a metered resource.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A seat has a price fixed at signature. A consumption event has a cost every
      time it runs. Managing the first while operating the second is a category
      error, and it is the reason the bill arrives on the provider’s schedule
      rather than the buyer’s.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-layers">
      <div>
        <p class="layer-name">AI Business Economics</p>
        <p class="layer-role">is the science.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="layer-name">AI Operations Management</p>
        <p class="layer-role">is the practice discipline that acts on it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-actions">
      {% if first_locked %}
      <a class="btn" href="{{ first_locked.slug }}/">Start reading: {{ first_locked.title }}</a>
      {% endif %}
      <a class="btn btn-quiet" href="#parts">See the structure</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="parts">
    <div class="band-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Inside the book</p>
      <h2>Four parts, {{ chapter_count }} chapters</h2>
      <p class="band-meta">{{ locked_count }} of {{ chapter_count }} published</p>
    </div>
    <div class="parts-grid">
      {% for p in book %}
      <article class="part-card">
        <p class="part-numeral" aria-hidden="true">{{ p.numeral }}</p>
        <p class="eyebrow">Part {{ p.numeral }}</p>
        <h3>{{ p.name }}</h3>
        <p class="part-purpose">{{ p.purpose }}</p>
        <ol class="part-chapters">
          {% for c in p.chapters %}
          <li>
            {% if c.locked %}
            <a href="{{ c.slug }}/"><span class="ch-n">{{ c.number }}</span> {{ c.title }}</a>
            {% else %}
            <span class="soon"><span class="ch-n">{{ c.number }}</span> {{ c.title }}</span>
            {% endif %}
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ol>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="read">
    <div class="band-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Read</p>
      <h2>Published chapters</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="toc-list">
      {% for p in book %}{% for c in p.chapters %}{% if c.locked %}
      <li>
        <a href="{{ c.slug }}/">
          <span class="toc-num">Part {{ p.numeral }} &middot; Chapter {{ c.number }}</span>
          <span class="toc-title">{{ c.title }}</span>
        </a>
        <span class="toc-part">{{ p.name }}</span>
      </li>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
    </ol>
    <p class="note-line">Chapters appear here as they lock. A chapter is published
       only after it has passed thirteen steps, including two independent source
       and fact checks.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="editions">
    <div class="band-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Editions</p>
      <h2>The text is free to read here</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="editions">
      <div class="edition">
        <h3>This website</h3>
        <p>The complete text of every published chapter, with its sources.</p>
        <p class="price">Free</p>
      </div>
      <div class="edition">
        <h3>Print and ebook</h3>
        <p>The typeset book, plus the apparatus this site does not carry: the
           theorem and lemma appendix, the capstone dataset, problem solutions,
           and instructor materials.</p>
        <p class="price">In preparation</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

<footer class="foot" data-chrome>
  <div class="foot-inner">
    <p>AI Operations Management. Daniel S. Wipert, Chorus AI Systems.</p>
    <p>{{ locked_count }} of {{ chapter_count }} chapters published.</p>
  </div>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
